Thus steps for each schedule_candidate:

- create_candidate
- allocate_vehicle_unit (choose a vehicle unit; we have three vehicles; we can reuse but need to ensure not already allocated; after each dispatch we release vehicle via execute_schedule_dispatch effect which makes vehicle_available again. So we can reuse same vehicle for multiple candidates sequentially.)
- attach_task_profile
- confirm_candidate_preparedness
- assign_operator_resource
- apply_operational_constraint (requires operational_constraint_available, candidate_operational_constraint_linked, not constraint_applied)
- confirm_operator_alignment (requires constraint_applied, candidate_operator_linked, not operator_alignment_confirmed)
- assign_compliance_certificate (requires compliance_certificate_available)
- verify_compliance_certificate (requires operator_alignment_confirmed, candidate_compliance_certificate_linked, not compliance_validation_complete)
- finalize_candidate_after_compliance_validation (requires compliance_validation_complete, not candidate_finalized) -> sets dispatch_ready and candidate_finalized.

After that, we allocate dispatch slot (allocate_dispatch_slot_for_candidate) requiring dispatch_ready, candidate_task_profile_linked, dispatch_slot_available, not dispatch_allocated.

Then execute_schedule_dispatch.

